{"type":"standard","title":"Kugama language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Kugama language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q3913307","titles":{"canonical":"Kugama_language","normalized":"Kugama language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Kugama language</span></span>"},"pageid":35269109,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1330600060","tid":"c76a439a-e704-11f0-a0ef-ab63705f47de","timestamp":"2026-01-01T11:26:56Z","description":"Adamawa language spoken in Nigeria","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kugama_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kugama_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kugama_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Kugama_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kugama_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Kugama_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kugama_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Kugama_language"}},"extract":"Kugama, also known as Wam (Wã̀m) or Gengle, is an Adamawa language of Nigeria. It is spoken in Mayo-Belwa and Fufore Local Government Areas of Adamawa State. It is classified within the Yendang group of the Adamawa language family.","extract_html":"<p><b>Kugama</b>, also known as <b>Wam</b> (<i>Wã̀m</i>) or <b>Gengle</b>, is an Adamawa language of Nigeria. It is spoken in Mayo-Belwa and Fufore Local Government Areas of Adamawa State. It is classified within the Yendang group of the Adamawa language family.</p>"}